1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-3--3c-core-listening-skills","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-3/3c-core-listening-skills","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-3/3c-core-listening-skills","sourceHash":"bf36ba7a18e762c703e8feaec6d3695e7a248c98d67f0a2306a1943e7db9defd","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:49.938Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"3C — Core Listening Skills","zh":"3C — 核心听力技能"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your listening has improved significantly — you've narrowed the reading-listening gap, chosen a dialect, and you can follow a lot of what's said in familiar content without subtitles.","zh":"你的听力已经显著提升——你缩小了阅读与听力之间的差距，选定了方言，而且在熟悉的内容中，即使没有字幕，也能听懂很多内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But there are still moments where fast speech, mumbled words, or unfamiliar phrasing trips you up. This sub-phase is about targeted training to sharpen your ears.","zh":"但快速语 speech、含混不清的词语或不熟悉的措辞仍会让你在某些时候跟不上。这一子阶段的重点是进行有针对性的训练，磨练你的听辨能力。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Think of it as going to the listening gym. The exercises here are deliberately harder than normal immersion. They force your brain to work at the edge of its ability, which is exactly what makes you faster and more accurate. It can be mentally exhausting — that's a sign it's working.","zh":"把它想象成去听力健身房。这里的练习会刻意比普通沉浸更难，迫使大脑在能力边缘运转，而这正是让你变得更快、更准确的关键。练习可能会让你感到精神疲惫——这说明它正在发挥作用。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Sentence mining and other vocabulary focused activities are significantly reduced here so that you can put all focus on listening. Jumping into pure reading (just text, no audio) can be a great supplement (and break from the mind-melting listening practice). <a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">Extensive Reading</a>","zh":"句子挖掘和其他以词汇为重点的活动在这里会大幅减少，以便你把全部注意力放在听力上。加入纯阅读（只有文字、没有音频）可以作为很好的补充，也能让你从令人头昏脑涨的听力练习中获得片刻放松。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">泛读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of this sub-phase, you should be able to sit down and watch a TV show made for adults, without subtitles or tools, and enjoy it.","zh":"在这一子阶段结束时，你应该能够坐下来观看面向成年人的电视节目，不使用字幕或工具，并且享受其中。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Transcription</strong> — Listen to a short audio clip and write down exactly what you hear, word for word. Then check your work against a transcript. This is one of the most powerful listening exercises because it forces you to hear every single word — not just the ones your brain picks up naturally. It's also brutally revealing: you'll discover sounds you've been mishearing, words that blend together, and patterns you've been glossing over. Start with short clips and gradually increase length. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/transcription\">Transcription</a>","zh":"<strong>听写</strong>——听一小段音频，逐字准确地写下你听到的内容，然后将答案与文字稿进行核对。这是最有效的听力练习之一，因为它迫使你听清每一个词，而不只是大脑自然捕捉到的词。它也会毫不留情地暴露问题：你会发现自己一直听错的声音、连在一起的词，以及被你忽略的语言模式。从短片段开始，再逐渐增加长度。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/transcription\">听写</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Listen Looping</strong> — When you encounter a section of audio that's hard to understand but feels like it <em>should</em> be understandable, loop it. Play it over and over, focusing your ears on the specific words and sounds. This trains your brain to parse fast, connected speech. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/listen-looping\">Listen Looping</a>","zh":"<strong>循环听</strong>——当你遇到一段难以理解、但感觉<em>应该</em>能够理解的音频时，就把它循环播放。反复播放，集中注意力辨听其中具体的词语和声音。这会训练大脑解析快速、连贯的语音。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/listen-looping\">循环听</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Intensive Listening continues</strong> — You're still doing intensive listening from 3A, but by now you should need to pause and check subtitles much less often. The goal is for this to gradually merge with freeflow — you're listening at full speed, and only occasionally need to go back and check something. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/intensive-listening\">Intensive Listening</a>","zh":"<strong>强化听力仍在继续</strong>——你仍在进行3A阶段的强化听力，但现在应该不需要经常暂停和查看字幕了。目标是让强化听力逐渐与自由流听力融合：以正常速度听，只偶尔回去确认某些内容。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/intensive-listening\">强化听力</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Listening grows</strong> — As your ears improve, more of your immersion time shifts to freeflow. This is where you're just consuming content for enjoyment without stopping. The more you do this, the more natural the language sounds. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/freeflow-listening\">Freeflow Listening</a>","zh":"<strong>自由流听力增加</strong>——随着听辨能力提高，你会将更多沉浸时间转向自由流听力。这时你只需为了享受而消费内容，不再频繁停下来。这样做得越多，语言听起来就越自然。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/freeflow-listening\">自由流听力</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Extensive Reading (optional)</strong> — As you spend more time on listening, you don't want to neglect the power of reading! Starting to read novels (even easy ones) is a fantastic way to grow your vocabulary and processing of the language's grammar. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">Extensive Reading</a>","zh":"<strong>泛读（可选）</strong>——当你把更多时间花在听力上时，也不要忽视阅读的力量！开始阅读小说（即使是简单的小说）是扩大词汇量、提高语法处理能力的绝佳方式。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/extensive-reading\">泛读</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming drops further as listening practice dominates: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"随着听力练习占据主导地位，语言预热进一步减少：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>50%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>40%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 10 mins","zh":"词汇学习：10分钟"},{"en":"Transcription: 10 mins","zh":"听写：10分钟"},{"en":"Listen Looping: 10 mins","zh":"循环听：10分钟"},{"en":"Intensive Listening: 20 mins","zh":"强化听力：20分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 30 mins","zh":"自由流听力：30分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow reading: 20 mins","zh":"自由流阅读：20分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 3D when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入3D："}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Can enjoy and follow most of an adult TV show without subtitles or tools","zh":"无需字幕或工具，也能享受并看懂成人电视节目中的大部分内容"},{"en":"Understand the vast majority of what's said in content within your chosen domain and dialect","zh":"能够理解所选领域和方言的内容中绝大多数表达"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The intensive listening exercises in this sub-phase are based on principles from skill acquisition theory and perceptual learning. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780203628942\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DeKeyser (2007, 2015)</a> explains that language skills progress from controlled (conscious, attention-demanding) processing to automatic (unconscious, effortless) processing through extended practice. When you do transcription or listen looping — repeating the same audio until you can parse it correctly — you're deliberately working at the edge of your current ability, which is precisely the condition that drives this shift from controlled to automatic processing.","zh":"这一子阶段的强化听力练习基于技能习得理论和知觉学习的原则。<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780203628942\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DeKeyser（2007、2015）</a>解释说，语言技能会通过长期练习，从受控加工（有意识、需要集中注意力）发展为自动化加工（无意识、毫不费力）。进行听写或循环听时——反复播放同一段音频，直到能够正确解析——你是在有意识地挑战当前能力的边缘，而这正是推动受控加工转向自动化加工的关键条件。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
